832	/// (F09-5) The body a QUEUED event is sent with: the event re-built field by field through the
833	/// closed classes, in the constructors' key order - the allowlist of
834	/// [`crate::telemetry::Event`] (a consultation) or [`crate::telemetry::RatingEvent`] (a rating),
835	/// every string a closed value: the engine one of [`ENGINES`]; the provider a CLASS of the table
836	/// (a roster label - `customer-acme` - is `other`); the model an entry of that class's list (else
837	/// `other`, `unknown` kept); the purpose, the outcome, the mark, the judge, `os` and the versions
838	/// through their own closed sets; ids only of their own shapes (`consult_ref` a guid, the instance
839	/// a SHA-256). An event C3 queued before wave 2 (the raw event, its labels as typed) leaves with
840	/// `other` where its labels were; an event of the current constructors closes to itself. `None` -
841	/// the event is discarded, with a local diagnostic - for a body that is no C3 consultation or rating
842	/// event, or that has no instance id or no time of this client's shape (nothing could attribute it).
843	///
844	/// (wave 2g, F19-3) What leaves is ALWAYS the serialised reconstruction, never the queued bytes: a
845	/// body can hide a value the parse dropped - a duplicate key (`"title":"customer-acme"` before the
846	/// real `title`: the parse keeps the last one), whitespace, escapes - so even a body whose parsed
847	/// value equals its reconstruction is re-serialised. The reconstruction keeps the constructors' key
848	/// order (`preserve_order`), so a current event still leaves byte for byte as it was built.
849	pub(crate) fn close_event_body(body: &str) -> Option<String> {
850	    let v: Value = serde_json::from_str(body).ok()?;
851	    close_event(&v).map(|closed| closed.to_string())
852	}
