{
  "schema_version": "1",
  "verdict": "ADVISE",
  "verdict_reason": "Framing review of two measurement designs before implementation; several premises of the sketch (window-share attribution, hook visibility, one outcome vocabulary) are contradicted or untested in the evidence, so the design should be revised before the closed vocabulary is published.",
  "reply_markdown": "**Framing.** The sketch treats the vocabulary as the hard commitment and the score as later work. Invert it: scores will be revised many times, so publish only raw closed measures (with `unknown` for what a host cannot see) and derive every score nightly. Two premises are shaky: (i) window share is not attributable — the 5-hour window moved 8→72 % with no run of ours (state.md 11:57) and 260k tokens moved it 30→65 % (09:02); (ii) usefulness is confounded — hard tasks get high effort, so high effort will look worse. To choose I need: how often accounts have other consumers; whether z.ai has a fourth tier on glm-5.3; what SubagentStop really carries; and the install count (below ~50, per-tier tables stay noise).\n\n**Q1.** gpt-6-astra: chore low, reading/digest **medium** (a cheap digest poisons the judge), checkpoint medium, diff-review high, acceptance high, core-contract/stuck xhigh. glm-5.3: scout low, checkpoint/diff-review/acceptance high, max only for stuck/core-contract or as second judge on disagreement — GLM is the cheap, window-free workhorse; move non-acceptance to it. Express roster policy as **presets or floor/cap**, never endpoint tiers: z.ai maps medium→high and xhigh→max, so \"checkpoint medium\" is high on GLM; events must carry `effort` (sent) and `effort_requested` (preset) or the table compares incomparable tiers. Denominator: a **vector**, not a scalar — confirmed findings per window-share-point, per money, per wall-minute; score window share only when the run's own delta explains the movement. Unlisted designs: (a) raw-only schema + nightly derived scores (revisable without a break); (b) randomised exploration — 10–20 % of runs one tier off policy, flagged `effort_source: explore`; (c) paired judging — same digest at high and xhigh; disagreement rate is the top tier's marginal value; (d) effort ratchet — escalate only on empty/invalid reply.\n\n**Q2.** SubagentStop is the right *closing* point, but pair it with SubagentStart: a worker dying with the host emits nothing, so error shares are survivorship-biased (next start closes an orphan as `unknown`). The hook sees the **agent definition name**, not model or effort: tier from the name (closed list), model through CLAUDE_MODELS, `effort` + `effort_source: hook|transcript|rate|unknown` — `workers rate --effort` must never silently claim what the hook did not see. Never send: prompts, briefs, paths, transcript/session ids, agent labels as typed (custom names carry customer names → map or `other`), free-text notes, verification pattern names (boolean only). Attribution under rework: a pseudonymous `wave_ref` per wave, per-worker `useful` marks and credited-finding **counts** (no ids); a reworked worker is `partly` by definition and the rework is its own event; `verified` stays the objective signal; wave success is never inferred from worker outcome. Other hosts fit only if `other`/`unknown` is first-class, not a degradation.\n\n**Q3.** Consult: `effort`, `effort_requested`, `effort_source`, `effort_mapping`, `quota_cost` **bucketed** (exact percentages leak account size). Rating: `findings_confirmed` / `findings_implemented` counts at rating time — alternative 3's join without intake-side ids. New `worker` event: host, tier, model, effort, effort_source, duration bucket, outcome class, token/tool/edits buckets, `verified`, `resumes`, `wave_ref`. All optional-with-`unknown`, additive: `close_event` must keep events missing new fields (old clients) and must stop discarding non-consultation|rating types (classes.rs:870). No derived scores, no free text; never reuse the intake's free-text `agent_report`.\n\n**Q4.** Scout-and-judge fails on compression loss and anchoring — a confident wrong digest is worse than none. Caps: (1) digest = **map**, not summary — one line per changed file, no correctness claims; (2) ≤40 lines / 4 KB with machine-checked **coverage** — every diffstat file appears once or the digest is discarded and the judge gets raw; (3) the judge always gets diffstat + file list + ≤N raw-hunk requests (one budgeted call); (4) the judge's cap is in **calls** (1 + ≤2 escalations on empty/invalid replies) — the window is not token-linear; (5) audit arm: 1 in 5 judgings gets the raw diff; the confirmed-finding gap measures digest loss. A blocker claim must quote a raw path:line.\n\n## Requested checks\n- **RC1** (finding #2) — cwd: the xelth.com repo. Read `docs/t-hub` and the intake's event parser. Read-only, 30 min. Settles whether unknown `event_type`/details fields are dropped, 400-refused or stored; the worker event's phasing depends on it.\n- **RC2** (Q1) — cwd: this repo. One `c3 consult` chore to z.ai glm-5.3 with `--native-effort xhigh`; observe accept/refuse and ledger `effort_confirmed`. Workspace-write (small quota cost), 5 min. Settles the fourth-tier question.\n- **RC3** (Q2) — cwd: scratch. SubagentStart/Stop hooks dumping stdin JSON to a temp file; run one Task with a haiku agent and an explicit effort override. Workspace-write, 10 min. Settles whether the payload carries model/effort or only the agent name.\n- **RC4** (finding #3) — cwd: this machine. Script over `~/.codex/sessions` rollouts: per-run window deltas vs total window movement. Read-only, 20 min. Settles the attributable share of window consumption.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "locations": [
        {"path": ".collab/consilium-2026-10-14/handoffs/01-claude-measure-reviewers-and-workers.md", "line": 59},
        {"path": ".collab/parity-0.6.1-2026-10-08/state.md", "line": 128}
