        {"path": "crates/c3/src/telemetry/event.rs", "line": 58}
      ],
      "claim": "The proposed tier score (usefulness per 5-hour-window share) is not computable from published telemetry (the event carries tokens but no quota cost) and is biased where it is computable: the window moved 8->72 % without our runs (another consumer) and 260k tokens moved it 30->65 % (non-linear), so per-run window share is both unattributable and non-monotone in effort.",
      "trigger": "Aggregating usefulness per window share at the intake from current event fields.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "read-code", "reference": ".collab/parity-0.6.1-2026-10-08/state.md:208", "observation": "window 8 % -> 72 % between 11:18 and 11:55 WITHOUT our runs; another consumer on the account"},
        {"kind": "read-code", "reference": ".collab/parity-0.6.1-2026-10-08/state.md:184", "observation": "window went 30 -> 65 % for 260k tokens inside one round - non-linear"},
